.TH MQ_NOTIFY 3 "2026-07-01" "Substrate" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
mq_notify \- register for notification when a message arrives on an empty queue
.SH LIBRARY
Realtime library (librt, \-lrt)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <mqueue.h>
.PP
.BI "int mq_notify(mqd_t " mqdes ", const struct sigevent *" sevp );
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR mq_notify ()
arranges for the calling process to be notified when a message is delivered
to the empty queue
.IR mqdes .
Only one process may be registered for notification on a queue at a time.
.PP
The notification is described by
.RB * sevp ,
a
.B struct sigevent
whose
.I sigev_notify
member is one of:
.TP
.B SIGEV_SIGNAL
Deliver the signal
.I sigev_signo
to the process when a message arrives on the previously empty queue.
.TP
.B SIGEV_THREAD
Invoke
.I sigev_notify_function
in a new thread.  (Realized in librt by an internal helper.)
.TP
.B SIGEV_NONE
Register the process without delivering any notification.
.PP
Notification occurs only when the queue transitions from empty to non-empty
.I and
no other process is blocked in
.BR mq_receive (3)
on the queue at that moment: a waiting receiver takes the message instead.
The registration is one-shot \(em it is removed as soon as notification is
delivered, when the registered process closes the descriptor, or when the
queue is unlinked.  A subsequent
.BR mq_notify ()
must be issued to re-register.
.PP
If
.I sevp
is NULL and the calling process is currently registered, its registration is
removed.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success 0 is returned.  On error \-1 is returned and
.I errno
is set.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EBADF
.I mqdes
is not a valid message-queue descriptor.
.TP
.B EBUSY
Another process is already registered for notification on the queue.
.TP
.B EINVAL
.I sigev_notify
is
.B SIGEV_SIGNAL
with an invalid
.IR sigev_signo .
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
static volatile sig_atomic_t got;
static void handler(int s) { (void)s; got = 1; }

signal(SIGUSR1, handler);
struct sigevent sev = { 0 };
sev.sigev_notify = SIGEV_SIGNAL;
sev.sigev_signo  = SIGUSR1;
mq_notify(q, &sev);
/* got becomes 1 once a message arrives on the empty queue */
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mq_open (3),
.BR mq_send (3),
.BR mq_receive (3),
.BR sigevent (3)
